<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Cybersecurity Tips Everyone Should Know</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.0.0/css/all.min.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../css/blog.css">
</head>

<body>
    <%- include("../partials/navbar", { activePage }) %>
    <main class="article-container">
        <article class="blog-post">
            <h1 class="post-title"> Cybersecurity Tips Everyone Should Know </h1>
            <div class="post-meta"> <span> <i class="fas fa-user"></i> Published by: Sophia Williams </span> <span> <i
                        class="fas fa-calendar-alt"></i> Date: 10.04.2026 </span> <span> <i class="fas fa-tag"></i>
                    Category: Cybersecurity </span> </div>
            <div class="post-hero-image"> <img src="../img/security.jpg"
                    alt="Cybersecurity protection and digital security"> </div>
            <div class="post-content">
                <p> Cybersecurity threats continue to evolve, making digital safety important for every internet user.
                    Personal accounts, financial information and private documents can become targets when basic
                    security practices are ignored. </p>
                <p> Strong and unique passwords are the first line of defense. Reusing the same password across several
                    websites allows one compromised account to place many other accounts at risk. </p>
                <p> Multi-factor authentication adds another security layer by requiring an additional verification
                    step. Even when a password is stolen, an attacker may still be unable to access the protected
                    account. </p>
                <p> Software updates should be installed regularly because they often contain important security fixes.
                    Outdated applications, browsers and operating systems may contain vulnerabilities that are already
                    known to attackers. </p>
                <p> Users should also remain cautious when opening unexpected emails, attachments or links. Messages
                    that create urgency, request passwords or promise unrealistic rewards may be phishing attempts. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="author-actions">
                <a href="../blog-create" class="btn-action btn-edit"> Edit Post </a>
                <button type="button" class="btn-action btn-delete"> Delete Post </button>
            </div>
        </article>
        <hr class="section-divider">
        <section class="comments-section">
            <h2>Comments:</h2>
            <div class="comments-list">
                <div class="comment-card">
                    <div class="comment-header"> <span class="comment-author">Chris</span> <span
                            class="comment-date">April 12, 2026</span> </div>
                    <p class="comment-text"> Everyone should enable two-factor authentication. It only takes a few
                        minutes and provides much better protection. </p>
                </div>
                <div class="comment-card">
                    <div class="comment-header"> <span class="comment-author">Anna</span> <span
                            class="comment-date">April 13, 2026</span> </div>
                    <p class="comment-text"> Simple but useful security tips. Password reuse is still a very common
                        problem among many users. </p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-form">
                <h3>Leave a Reply</h3>
                <div class="form-group"> <textarea placeholder="Write your comment here..." rows="4"
                        required></textarea> </div> <button type="button" class="btn-submit-comment"> Submit Comment
